# Owner: M1
# NOTE (M3): updated to match the real variable names used by server/utils/db.ts
# and the working .env the team is running against — the old NUXT_DATABASE_URL /
# NUXT_AUTH_SECRET names were placeholders. Please fold this back in / adjust if
# you settle on different names, just keep server/utils/db.ts in sync.
#
# NOTE (M3, Day 4): if you see `querySrv ECONNREFUSED _mongodb._tcp....`
# on startup, db.ts already tries to fix it by switching Node's DNS resolver
# to Google/Cloudflare (which support SRV lookups). If that still doesn't
# work on your network (some locked-down networks block outbound DNS/27017
# entirely), get the non-SRV connection string instead: in Atlas, go to
# Database > Connect > Drivers, then use the "Standard connection string"
# option (not the default SRV one). It looks like this — three explicit
# hosts, port 27017 each, no "+srv", with tls/authSource/replicaSet added:
#   MONGODB_URI=mongodb://<user>:<pass>@shard-00-00.xxxxx.mongodb.net:27017,shard-00-01.xxxxx.mongodb.net:27017,shard-00-02.xxxxx.mongodb.net:27017/?ssl=true&replicaSet=<replicaSetName>&authSource=admin&retryWrites=true&w=majority
# (host names, replica set name, and the db name are specific to your own
# cluster — copy them from Atlas rather than reusing another project's.)
MONGODB_URI=
MONGODB_DB=insightflow
AUTH_USERNAME=
AUTH_PASSWORD=
SESSION_SECRET=
NUXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
